* Timer models for KiCad/ngspice.
* Repository-authored nominal NE555 approximation, not a TI SPICE model.
* Reference: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/ne555.pdf (SLFS022K).
* Public terminals follow physical PDIP-8 pin order.
* See MODEL_SOURCES.md and docs/TIMERS.md for validation and limitations.
*
.SUBCKT NE555P VSS TRIG OUT RESET CONT THRES DISCH VCC
* The three 5 kohm resistors expose the control-voltage input and its loading.
R_TOP VCC CONT 5k
R_MID CONT LOW 5k
R_BOTTOM LOW VSS 5k
* Smooth comparators and a regenerative analog latch need no XSPICE library.
* RESET dominates TRIG; TRIG dominates THRES, as in TI's function table.
B_SET SET VSS V=0.5*(1+tanh(V(LOW,TRIG)/1m))
B_CLEAR CLEAR VSS V=0.5*(1+tanh(V(THRES,CONT)/1m))
B_RUN RUN VSS V=0.5*(1+tanh((V(RESET,VSS)-0.7)/10m))
B_MEMORY MEMORY VSS V=V(RUN,VSS)*(V(SET,VSS)+(1-V(SET,VSS))*(1-V(CLEAR,VSS))*0.5*(1+tanh(20*(V(STATE,VSS)-0.5))))
R_MEMORY MEMORY STATE 1k
C_MEMORY STATE VSS 50p
B_Q Q VSS V=0.5*(1+tanh(20*(V(STATE,VSS)-0.5)))
* Bipolar output approximation: 1.4 V source headroom, finite resistance and
* soft 200 mA current limits. Load currents flow through the supply terminals.
B_SOURCE VCC OUT I=V(Q,VSS)*0.2*tanh(max(V(VCC,OUT)-1.4,0)/0.6)
B_SINK OUT VSS I=(1-V(Q,VSS))*0.2*tanh(V(OUT,VSS)/3)
R_OUT OUT VSS 100meg
* Effective edge-shaping capacitance, not a measured package capacitance.
C_OUT OUT VSS 1n
B_DISCTL DISCTL VSS V=1-V(Q,VSS)
S_DIS DISCH VSS DISCTL VSS DIS_SWITCH
.MODEL DIS_SWITCH SW(RON=18 ROFF=10G VT=0.5 VH=0.05)
* Approximate no-load supply current, including the divider at nominal CONT.
B_BIAS VCC VSS I=max(0,(0.0007-1/15000)*V(VCC,VSS)-0.0015+0.001*(1-V(Q,VSS)))
.ENDS NE555P
